# Shape of infra/mcp/secrets.sops.yaml (the ENCRYPTED file). NO real values here.
#
# Create/edit the encrypted file directly so no plaintext copy ever exists on disk:
#   sops edit infra/mcp/secrets.sops.yaml          # uses the .sops.yaml age recipient; encrypts on save
# Do not `cp` this file to secrets.sops.yaml and fill it in plaintext. If you must cp, run
#   sops --encrypt --in-place infra/mcp/secrets.sops.yaml
# immediately, BEFORE putting the real value in (then use `sops edit`).
#
# Only the OAuth client SECRET lives here. client_id is not secret: it is in infra/mcp/servers.yaml.
# Keys are env var names so they can be injected directly (see infra/README.md).
GOOGLE_MCP_CLIENT_SECRET: REPLACE_ME
